WEBVTT

00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:12.450
Through numerous unifications and break ups, the number of interstellar nations continued to decrease...

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:18.890
...until only four nations remained excluding the Humankind Empire Abh.

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:27.870
Ranked according to power, these four nations are the United Mankind, the Federation of Hania,

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:36.180
the Republic of Greater Alcont, and the People's Sovereign Union of Planets.

00:00:36.190 --> 00:00:46.520
Twelve years ago, the four nations gathered in Nova Sicily and entered into
an agreement setting aside the grudges that they had with one another.

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:51.730
This was the Nova Sicily Treaty military alliance.

00:00:51.730 --> 00:01:00.200
The member nations of this alliance are officially called the Nations of the Nova Sicily Treaty Structure,

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:03.570
more commonly known as the Four Nations Alliance.

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:15.490
Although it was not clear what the objective of the alliance was, it was
obvious that the alliance was formed to counter the only nation
not included in the pact.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:20.320
The Humankind Empire Abh.

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:55.310
Déucrémhoth

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:55.310
Surprise Attack

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:01.230
Captain.

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:02.030
Yes?

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:03.930
Please come to the bridge immediately.

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:06.710
We've sighted unidentified space-time bubbles.

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:07.800
I'll be right there.

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:16.210
Lairia, what's the status?

00:03:17.390 --> 00:03:19.350
Direction, 78 degrees ahead...

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:21.950
...distance, 1539.17 cédlairhs.

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:23.650
Their course is 18 degrees.

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:25.390
Sfagnomr is in that direction.

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:28.890
Sfagnomr is our next port-of-call, isn't it?

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:29.790
Yes, it is.

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:32.230
We should arrive there first.

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:33.670
And what's their size?

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:37.560
We've located 120 space-time bubbles...

00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:40.070
...of approximately 90 zaisacbau each.

00:03:40.270 --> 00:03:43.940
They would amount to a total output of 4 battle divisions.

00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:47.010
Do you know which saudec they entered from?

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:50.510
I have Leshikuria calculating that right now.

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:54.220
I've narrowed it down to 47...

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:55.760
...but I can't narrow it down any further.

00:03:56.020 --> 00:03:58.490
Are any of them presently in use?

00:03:59.130 --> 00:03:59.820
No.

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:03.190
These saudecs are all closed, and all generally neglected.

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:08.060
Are there any saudecs within a light year of inhabited planets?

00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:19.210
Not one.

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:22.210
Any within five light years?

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:32.630
There's one!

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:33.860
Where?

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:37.290
Four point one light years from Saudec Keish 193...

00:04:37.370 --> 00:04:40.330
...is Vascotton 4 of the Vascotton system.

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:41.800
That planet is occupied by...

00:04:43.910 --> 00:04:45.630
...the United Mankind.

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:50.310
The United Mankind...

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:00.850
<i>It's been five days since Gosroth set out.</i>

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:02.520
<i>At that time...</i>

00:05:02.590 --> 00:05:05.960
<i>...I was tackling the rules of the supply officer module.</i>

00:05:07.230 --> 00:05:07.790
It's impossible!

00:05:10.130 --> 00:05:11.620
This is totally impossible.

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:13.690
There's no way I can remember all this.

00:05:14.570 --> 00:05:18.530
There are 120 articles just on lunch manners!

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:22.600
Dourin was right.

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:23.940
<i>Well...</i>

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:27.110
<i>...you were commuting to an Abh school here, weren't you?</i>

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:29.440
<i>The school I went to was...</i>

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:32.350
<i>...for educating candidates expected to become...</i>

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:34.720
<i>...citizens of the Empire.</i>

00:05:34.990 --> 00:05:36.390
<i>There were no Abh.</i>

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:39.720
<i>Not even beautiful Abh teachers?</i>

00:05:40.530 --> 00:05:42.960
<i>The teachers were all grumpy men from the territories.</i>

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:49.400
<i>Why couldn't you just go to a school with Abh kids?</i>

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:51.970
<i>The Abh have no elementary school system.</i>

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:53.300
<i>Really?</i>

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:57.070
<i>Then how do they learn how to read and write?</i>

00:05:57.550 --> 00:06:00.140
<i>I hear the parents teach them all that.</i>

00:06:00.650 --> 00:06:01.510
<i>But...</i>

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:06.340
<i>...there was no way my father could've taught me like the Abh.</i>

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:07.390
<i>That's why...</i>

00:06:07.460 --> 00:06:10.790
<i>...I got shipped off to that school if only to...</i>

00:06:10.860 --> 00:06:13.090
<i>...learn the Abh language and basics.</i>

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:16.530
<i>And that took a whole 7 years?</i>

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:22.070
<i>I always thought you were pretty smart...</i>

00:06:22.140 --> 00:06:23.760
<i>...but I guess I was wrong.</i>

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:28.040
He was right.

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:32.540
So, this is it.

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:33.910
What is it?

00:06:34.650 --> 00:06:38.610
It seems like the Four Nations Alliance want to start a war.

00:06:38.690 --> 00:06:40.280
Don't you agree?

00:06:40.350 --> 00:06:42.450
They've been making unreasonable requests...

00:06:42.520 --> 00:06:44.680
...like advocating Haïder independence...

00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:47.520
...and demanding access to routes within the Empire...

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:51.050
...so they can maintain and defend their independence.

00:06:51.130 --> 00:06:55.130
They're well aware that the Empire would not agree to that.

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:56.060
Yes. And?

00:06:56.570 --> 00:06:58.130
In other words...

00:06:58.210 --> 00:07:01.640
...they're done preparing, and they want an excuse to attack.

00:07:02.010 --> 00:07:03.070
I see.

00:07:04.010 --> 00:07:07.110
A lot must've gone into this preparation.

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:09.680
They would've had to check out a number of saudecs...

00:07:09.690 --> 00:07:12.340
...throughout space to find one they could use.

00:07:12.550 --> 00:07:14.950
And even if they could find a suitable saudec...

00:07:15.020 --> 00:07:18.420
...they would've had to bring it in closer to them.

00:07:20.030 --> 00:07:21.150
To do that...

00:07:21.230 --> 00:07:25.030
...they would've had to wait years for the saudec to close again.

00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:29.060
If they managed to do that in less than ten years...

00:07:29.140 --> 00:07:31.430
...I'd say it was a miracle.

00:07:31.810 --> 00:07:33.100
Or...

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:35.370
...a nightmare.

00:07:41.950 --> 00:07:45.040
There's no question they were planning this well before...

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:46.520
...the establishment of Haïder.

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:47.580
Right.

00:07:47.660 --> 00:07:51.390
The problems with Haïder were just a recent coincidence.

00:07:51.590 --> 00:07:52.680
Moreover...

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:54.790
...the Nova Sicily Treaty might have come about...

00:07:54.860 --> 00:07:57.890
...for the purpose of carrying out these plans.

00:07:58.170 --> 00:07:59.630
Who knows.

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:03.760
Why bother telling such obvious lies.

00:08:04.370 --> 00:08:08.040
They're not fooling anyone else...

00:08:08.110 --> 00:08:09.600
...but themselves.

00:08:09.940 --> 00:08:11.880
Self-delusion?

00:08:12.280 --> 00:08:14.210
This is getting even more confusing.

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:17.880
I don't understand their way of thinking.

00:08:17.950 --> 00:08:21.910
But they probably believe what they're doing is just.

00:08:22.390 --> 00:08:24.360
What about our honor?

00:08:24.530 --> 00:08:26.990
We're seen as evil incarnate.

00:08:27.700 --> 00:08:30.990
Oh, didn't you know, Lairia?

00:08:31.170 --> 00:08:35.030
We're supposed to be natural born invaders and killers.

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:39.700
Take a look at any history book from the United Mankind.

00:08:39.770 --> 00:08:43.340
It blames virtually every disaster on the Abh.

00:08:44.410 --> 00:08:46.880
A change in the enemy's space-time bubbles!

00:08:48.050 --> 00:08:50.310
One space-time bubble has just split into ten.

00:08:51.020 --> 00:08:52.610
They've shifted their course toward us.

00:08:53.820 --> 00:08:54.810
From its size...

00:08:54.890 --> 00:08:57.550
...the space-time bubbles appear to correspond to each ship.

00:08:58.330 --> 00:09:01.660
How long until these visitors enter our mine field?

00:09:04.630 --> 00:09:07.600
They'll be entering at approximately 21:15.

00:09:08.370 --> 00:09:09.340
Executive officer.

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:11.170
Put us into combat status 2.

00:09:11.470 --> 00:09:13.410
At 20:30...

00:09:13.470 --> 00:09:15.970
...we'll go to combat status 1.

00:09:16.040 --> 00:09:16.600
Aye-aye.

00:09:17.380 --> 00:09:18.850
Senior Gunnery Officer...

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:19.850
...look into strategic options.

00:09:20.210 --> 00:09:21.150
Aye-aye.

00:09:21.820 --> 00:09:24.010
<i>What are our chances here?</i>

00:09:27.560 --> 00:09:28.250
What's that?!

00:09:28.390 --> 00:09:30.440
<i>This is the captain speaking.</i>

00:09:30.830 --> 00:09:32.520
<i>All personnel, listen carefully.</i>

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:35.320
<i>An unidentified space-time bubble...</i>

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:37.560
<i>...78 degrees and a distance of 1540 cédlairhs ahead of us...</i>

00:09:37.630 --> 00:09:40.190
<i>...is headed this way.</i>

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:42.500
<i>Their destination is assumed to be the same as ours...</i>

00:09:42.570 --> 00:09:45.000
<i>...that is, Sfagnomr.</i>

00:09:45.470 --> 00:09:48.370
<i>Listen carefully, boys and girls.</i>

00:09:48.910 --> 00:09:53.610
<i>At this rate, we're sure to arrive in Sfagnomr first.</i>

00:09:54.420 --> 00:09:57.510
<i>They don't seem too pleased about that...</i>

00:09:57.590 --> 00:10:02.330
<i>...and have sent 10 ship-size space-time bubbles toward us.</i>

00:10:02.760 --> 00:10:05.950
<i>We have yet to confirm where they came from...</i>

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:09.130
<i>...but they appear to be from the United Mankind.</i>

00:10:09.260 --> 00:10:11.860
<i>All personnel, it is likely that this will turn into a battle!</i>

00:10:12.030 --> 00:10:13.230
What's going on?

00:10:13.570 --> 00:10:15.330
<i>This is no drill.</i>

00:10:16.270 --> 00:10:17.400
I repeat.

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:19.130
This is no drill.

00:10:20.110 --> 00:10:22.080
If the enemy proves to be persistent...

00:10:22.240 --> 00:10:25.140
...we'll be going into battle...

00:10:25.210 --> 00:10:26.800
...at about 21:15.

00:10:27.010 --> 00:10:28.110
In preparation...

00:10:28.180 --> 00:10:29.950
...at exactly 20:30...

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:32.580
...we will go to combat status 1.

00:10:32.790 --> 00:10:36.150
All off-duty personnel are to rest up and be ready by this time.

00:10:36.960 --> 00:10:38.420
I will repeat one last time.

00:10:38.690 --> 00:10:42.650
Get this into your heads, my precious crew members.

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:45.730
This is not a drill or mock battle.

00:10:46.470 --> 00:10:48.030
This is your captain. Out.

00:10:49.400 --> 00:10:51.630
Going into battle...

00:10:58.610 --> 00:10:59.170
Lafiel.

00:10:59.980 --> 00:11:02.780
My orders are to take you to the bridge.

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:04.360
Can you come?

00:11:04.690 --> 00:11:06.310
What's going on, anyway?

00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:07.720
Just as you heard.

00:11:07.790 --> 00:11:10.190
I don't know any more than that.

00:11:12.130 --> 00:11:15.150
It looks like you joined us just as war was breaking out.

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:17.690
How fortunate.

00:11:17.830 --> 00:11:21.890
<i>Life sure is nothing but a string of good fortune.</i>

00:11:22.400 --> 00:11:24.560
<i>It takes no effort to hit a stumbling block.</i>

00:11:26.570 --> 00:11:30.170
I just hope it'll all be over before my appointment.

00:11:30.240 --> 00:11:31.730
That's not likely.

00:11:31.910 --> 00:11:35.250
We prefer not to end a war before there's a clear victor...

00:11:35.380 --> 00:11:38.750
...and the enemy appears to be the United Mankind.

00:11:39.320 --> 00:11:42.190
It's questionable whether it'll be over before I die.

00:11:42.790 --> 00:11:44.120
Your natural death?

00:11:44.690 --> 00:11:45.820
Yes.

00:11:45.890 --> 00:11:48.160
Maybe 200 or 250 years.

00:11:48.230 --> 00:11:49.990
In any case, until I die.

00:11:50.460 --> 00:11:54.700
You sure have a way of cheering people up.

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:02.010
I have brought His Excellency with me.

00:12:03.410 --> 00:12:06.210
I apologize for the trouble, Your Excellency.

00:12:07.850 --> 00:12:09.820
Flyer Trainee Abriel...

00:12:09.880 --> 00:12:11.370
...please remain as you are.

00:12:11.450 --> 00:12:12.280
Yes.

00:12:13.390 --> 00:12:15.180
Your Excellency...

00:12:15.320 --> 00:12:18.020
...I unfortunately cannot offer you a seat.

00:12:20.430 --> 00:12:21.990
It's quite alright.

00:12:22.060 --> 00:12:23.650
I can just stand.

00:12:24.530 --> 00:12:26.620
I'm sure you know what's happened...

00:12:26.630 --> 00:12:28.760
...from my announcement.

00:12:28.870 --> 00:12:29.600
Yes.

00:12:29.800 --> 00:12:31.740
Something about heading into battle.

00:12:31.970 --> 00:12:35.310
The probability of winning this battle is 37%.

00:12:36.080 --> 00:12:39.240
That's assuming the enemy is fighting with their best...

00:12:39.450 --> 00:12:42.880
...but even if they're just rookies on outdated ships...

00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:45.650
...our chances of winning still won't amount to 50%.

00:12:46.250 --> 00:12:47.780
That doesn't look too good.

00:12:48.090 --> 00:12:48.950
Right.

00:12:49.190 --> 00:12:51.380
Our best chance would be to flee...

00:12:51.890 --> 00:12:54.660
...but unfortunately our situation doesn't allow that.

00:12:55.560 --> 00:13:00.400
Therefore, I must have you disembark, Your Excellency.

00:13:00.730 --> 00:13:01.460
I see.

00:13:02.900 --> 00:13:05.030
This spaceship is equipped with a transfer shuttle.

00:13:05.440 --> 00:13:08.570
Although small, it is capable of planar space flight.

00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:12.380
Please go to Sfagnomr ahead of us on the shuttle.

00:13:12.910 --> 00:13:15.380
You'll need to refuel once while en route...

00:13:15.450 --> 00:13:18.650
...but you'll still arrive before that space-time bubble.

00:13:18.990 --> 00:13:21.610
You can then catch another ship.

00:13:21.890 --> 00:13:24.920
There's a communications base in Sfagnomr...

00:13:24.990 --> 00:13:28.050
...so you won't have to rely on luck to find a ship.

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:30.720
Flyer Trainee Abriel shall...

00:13:30.800 --> 00:13:33.230
...escort you to Sfagnomr.

00:13:34.470 --> 00:13:36.100
Captain! I couldn't!

00:13:38.310 --> 00:13:40.640
I have yet to earn a license to command a vessel.

00:13:40.810 --> 00:13:43.440
But you've completed the course for vessel command.

00:13:44.080 --> 00:13:47.050
You'll automatically receive your license after this passage.

00:13:47.110 --> 00:13:49.280
All that's left is paperwork.

00:13:49.350 --> 00:13:51.580
You are qualified, trainee.

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:53.910
But I'd like to remain on this ship and...

00:13:54.190 --> 00:13:57.210
I have no intention of arguing with a trainee.

00:13:58.430 --> 00:14:01.090
Am I not the captain of this ship?

00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:02.690
I don't understand.

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:04.560
Do I have to spell it out?

00:14:04.630 --> 00:14:06.360
I am an Abriel.

00:14:06.430 --> 00:14:09.030
I'd lose face as an Abriel if I run away from the enemy.

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:13.600
Quit your petty outbursts and your boasting...

00:14:13.670 --> 00:14:16.940
...at least until you've earned your wings...

00:14:17.880 --> 00:14:20.470
...Ablïarsec néïc Dubreuscr Bœrh Parhynr...

00:14:20.550 --> 00:14:21.540
...Lafiel!

00:14:21.950 --> 00:14:24.320
What do you mean by running away from the enemy?

00:14:24.390 --> 00:14:26.820
You're not attached to any of the battle divisions.

00:14:26.890 --> 00:14:28.480
You are still not ready.

00:14:28.560 --> 00:14:30.460
Nothing more than an extra body.

00:14:30.520 --> 00:14:32.890
Now, I gave you an order.

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:36.660
An important order to evacuate His Excellency, a non-combatant...

00:14:36.730 --> 00:14:39.020
...from the battle theater as well as to inform the Empire...

00:14:39.030 --> 00:14:42.470
...that we are being approached by what is likely an enemy fleet.

00:14:42.640 --> 00:14:46.500
Evading my order is an example of running away from the enemy.

00:14:46.970 --> 00:14:50.030
So ignorant that you don't know what running away is.

00:14:50.110 --> 00:14:51.870
If that's not losing face...

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:54.610
...then the Abriels are not worthy of Abh loyalty.

00:14:54.780 --> 00:14:57.720
If you still want to argue, I'll cite you for insubordination.

00:14:58.020 --> 00:15:01.450
You can discuss this further at the imperial tribunal.

00:15:10.400 --> 00:15:12.660
It was a misunderstanding on my part...

00:15:12.970 --> 00:15:14.020
...Captain.

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:16.370
As long as you realize that.

00:15:16.540 --> 00:15:19.530
Prepare to launch in the transfer shuttle at once.

00:15:19.970 --> 00:15:23.170
I still have something to discuss with His Excellency.

00:15:23.410 --> 00:15:24.100
Aye-aye.

00:15:24.410 --> 00:15:26.880
I will get right on with the launch preparations.

00:15:28.520 --> 00:15:30.070
Once you're ready to launch...

00:15:30.150 --> 00:15:31.850
...relay me a message.

00:15:32.620 --> 00:15:34.570
There's no need for you to return here.

00:15:38.060 --> 00:15:39.050
Aye-aye.

00:15:39.490 --> 00:15:40.260
As you wish.

00:15:40.930 --> 00:15:43.160
Now, go on.

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:48.300
I'll see you in Lacmhacarh...

00:15:48.640 --> 00:15:50.160
...my precious Royal Highness.

00:15:52.670 --> 00:15:54.440
Yes. Certainly.

00:16:03.450 --> 00:16:05.420
Your Excellency...

00:16:05.490 --> 00:16:07.920
...we are pressed for both time and space.

00:16:07.990 --> 00:16:11.630
Please take only the personal effects you absolutely need.

00:16:12.160 --> 00:16:13.680
I intend to do so.

00:16:13.990 --> 00:16:17.120
I'm sure l'll be able to collect the rest at the capital.

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:20.870
I must apologize for not being able to...

00:16:21.170 --> 00:16:22.690
...take you to the capital as planned.

00:16:23.040 --> 00:16:25.270
Transportation setbacks...

00:16:25.340 --> 00:16:27.310
...were not uncommon back in Bhorachr, either.

00:16:27.570 --> 00:16:30.330
Those kind words help set me at ease.

00:16:31.040 --> 00:16:32.880
By the way, Your Excellency...

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:34.880
Yes?

00:16:35.080 --> 00:16:37.310
In addition to your personal effects...

00:16:37.380 --> 00:16:39.720
...there's one other thing that I'd like you to take.

00:16:39.920 --> 00:16:40.440
Yes?

00:16:41.190 --> 00:16:42.680
Open weapons locker.

00:16:42.920 --> 00:16:46.540
This is Bomoüass Laicch Üémh Laubér Placïac.

00:17:07.780 --> 00:17:10.550
Please keep one for yourself...

00:17:10.620 --> 00:17:14.350
...and another for Flyer Trainee Abriel.

00:17:15.060 --> 00:17:17.920
She'll know how to use them.

00:17:18.930 --> 00:17:19.720
But...

00:17:19.790 --> 00:17:21.920
Why will we need something like this?

00:17:22.230 --> 00:17:23.920
You can't be too careful.

00:17:24.330 --> 00:17:27.930
I'm guessing that they're planning to attack us.

00:17:28.740 --> 00:17:33.540
They wouldn't be committing all that power just to stop us.

00:17:34.310 --> 00:17:35.100
But, you know...

00:17:35.180 --> 00:17:39.430
...I sense that they're seriously hell-bent on annihilating us.

00:17:39.670 --> 00:17:42.210
I can't help but feel that.

00:17:43.420 --> 00:17:44.820
You mean...

00:17:44.890 --> 00:17:47.380
...by the time we arrive in Sfagnomr...

00:17:47.450 --> 00:17:49.290
...the system may have surrendered to them.

00:17:50.060 --> 00:17:52.620
I pray that's not the case.

00:17:53.390 --> 00:17:54.760
Um...

00:17:54.830 --> 00:17:55.890
Captain.

00:17:55.960 --> 00:17:57.260
If your...

00:17:57.330 --> 00:18:00.860
...primary objective is to evacuate Her Royal Highness...

00:18:01.200 --> 00:18:04.340
...then wouldn't a guard be better?

00:18:06.370 --> 00:18:08.570
Please don't get me wrong.

00:18:08.880 --> 00:18:11.040
When I have non-combatants on-board...

00:18:11.110 --> 00:18:13.380
...my duty is to avoid battle as much as possible.

00:18:13.450 --> 00:18:15.210
If a battle cannot be avoided...

00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:17.680
...I take measures to ensure the non-combatants' safety.

00:18:17.950 --> 00:18:21.110
This is a responsibility of all Laburec commanders.

00:18:21.690 --> 00:18:26.420
It is a fact that Abriel is not a part of any battle division.

00:18:27.090 --> 00:18:31.030
Even if she had come from an average family...

00:18:31.700 --> 00:18:35.530
...I would've given her the task of piloting the shuttle.

00:18:37.540 --> 00:18:38.870
I'm sorry.

00:18:39.240 --> 00:18:41.140
That was a thoughtless question.

00:18:41.310 --> 00:18:42.610
On the other hand...

00:18:43.010 --> 00:18:46.240
...I'd be lying if I said the coincidence...

00:18:46.310 --> 00:18:49.100
...that the Her Royal Highness was also a pilot trainee didn't matter.

00:18:50.180 --> 00:18:53.130
You've given this a lot of thought, Captain.

00:18:53.620 --> 00:18:54.450
Sure.

00:18:54.760 --> 00:18:57.850
Although her royal status has no meaning in the military...

00:18:58.130 --> 00:19:01.790
...Her Highness Lafiel could one day become the Empress.

00:19:02.460 --> 00:19:06.020
She may even become a wise and great empress.

00:19:06.430 --> 00:19:07.730
When that day comes...

00:19:07.800 --> 00:19:11.720
...my hope is that she would reflect on her days here...

00:19:12.140 --> 00:19:14.160
...and acknowledge that she was taught well.

00:19:15.440 --> 00:19:18.280
I cannot allow her to die while she is still a child.

00:19:19.710 --> 00:19:20.580
That's very true.

00:19:21.180 --> 00:19:24.380
Well, you should be on your way now.

00:19:24.450 --> 00:19:26.680
Please return to your room and gather up your effects.

00:19:27.450 --> 00:19:30.180
I regret that no one's available to escort you...

00:19:30.590 --> 00:19:33.320
...but you do know your way to the flight deck?

00:19:33.390 --> 00:19:34.520
I'll be fine.

00:19:35.700 --> 00:19:36.820
Oh.

00:19:36.900 --> 00:19:39.530
About my family standard that you had placed in my room.

00:19:39.600 --> 00:19:41.400
I'll leave it behind for now.

00:19:41.470 --> 00:19:43.900
But I look forward to receiving it one day...

00:19:43.970 --> 00:19:45.200
...to commemorate my time on this ship.

00:19:45.470 --> 00:19:48.460
Spoken like a true nobleman, Your Excellency.

00:19:49.180 --> 00:19:51.410
Really? I'm glad.

00:19:56.450 --> 00:19:57.710
Well, Captain...

00:19:57.780 --> 00:19:58.610
I'll be going.

00:19:58.690 --> 00:20:00.310
Your Excellency...

00:20:00.390 --> 00:20:02.290
...please watch over Her Royal Highness.

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:04.520
I can't imagine such a desperate situation...

00:20:04.590 --> 00:20:07.960
...in which Her Highness would have to depend on me...

00:20:08.760 --> 00:20:11.130
But should such a time come, I'll do everything I can.

00:20:14.870 --> 00:20:16.770
The transfer shuttle is splitting into its own space-time.

00:20:18.440 --> 00:20:21.030
There go the young man and woman.

00:20:21.410 --> 00:20:23.630
I hope they don't encounter any difficulty.

00:20:24.040 --> 00:20:25.810
I certainly hope not.

00:20:26.050 --> 00:20:29.540
They both have quite unique backgrounds.

00:20:29.980 --> 00:20:33.180
They could be very interesting people in the future.

00:20:33.690 --> 00:20:36.650
Actually, they already are interesting people.

00:20:38.160 --> 00:20:39.280
You're right.

00:20:39.360 --> 00:20:43.350
Bringing them together may be my biggest accomplishment.

00:20:43.760 --> 00:20:44.790
But...

00:20:44.870 --> 00:20:49.460
...that's only possible if they reach the capital safely.

00:20:50.300 --> 00:20:52.900
You're quite concerned about those two, aren't you?

00:20:53.470 --> 00:20:55.660
Is it wrong to be concerned?

00:20:56.180 --> 00:20:57.170
No.

00:20:57.240 --> 00:21:02.270
But when you think about it, we're the ones in real danger.

00:21:02.950 --> 00:21:06.110
We really don't have the time to worry about others.

00:21:06.620 --> 00:21:09.380
Although I do feel wretched about questioning my superior.

00:21:09.790 --> 00:21:14.220
Knowing that you feel wretched when you question your superior...

00:21:14.660 --> 00:21:17.220
...is a nice thing to know.

00:21:17.760 --> 00:21:18.360
However...

00:21:19.200 --> 00:21:20.630
...you're absolutely right.

00:21:20.900 --> 00:21:23.700
This is when I must carry out my duty to my crew.

00:21:28.810 --> 00:21:30.240
<i>I've gotta say something.</i>

00:21:31.580 --> 00:21:34.650
<i>"I've gotta say something..." is all I kept thinking.</i>

00:21:37.920 --> 00:21:40.750
<i>Traveling in this craft through this separate universe...</i>

00:21:40.820 --> 00:21:43.220
<i>...we are the only two intelligent beings in space.</i>

00:21:44.320 --> 00:21:45.920
<i>One half...</i>

00:21:45.990 --> 00:21:48.790
<i>...is wallowing in a deep depression.</i>

00:21:49.500 --> 00:21:51.400
<i>And the other half...</i>

00:21:51.470 --> 00:21:52.760
<i>...is thinking desperately...</i>

00:21:52.830 --> 00:21:58.270
<i>...about how to brighten up the mood in this lonely separate universe.</i>

00:22:05.410 --> 00:22:06.740
Lafiel...

00:22:12.050 --> 00:22:12.850
Captain.

00:22:14.020 --> 00:22:15.950
We're within hailing range...

00:22:16.020 --> 00:22:17.850
...of the unidentified space-time bubble.

00:22:19.460 --> 00:22:21.290
Declare ourselves to them...

00:22:21.360 --> 00:22:23.230
...and get them to identify themselves.

00:22:23.300 --> 00:22:23.850
Aye-aye.

00:22:24.170 --> 00:22:26.670
This is the patrol ship Gosroth.

00:22:26.670 --> 00:22:30.130
Declare the name of your ship as well as your origin.

00:22:38.980 --> 00:22:39.760
Nothing yet?

00:22:40.050 --> 00:22:41.100
Quiet.

00:22:45.420 --> 00:22:46.850
We have a response.

00:22:51.190 --> 00:22:52.120
Why, this is...

00:22:58.200 --> 00:22:59.830
This is no correspondence.

00:23:00.470 --> 00:23:01.990
This is a challenge to battle!

00:24:32.330 --> 00:24:33.520
That confirms it.

00:24:35.400 --> 00:24:36.450
Hey...

00:24:36.530 --> 00:24:38.000
Lafiel...

00:24:46.070 --> 00:24:47.940
I was useless...

00:24:48.010 --> 00:24:50.140
...at such an important time.

00:24:51.540 --> 00:24:52.570
Don't say that!

00:24:54.850 --> 00:24:56.280
Commence battle!

00:24:56.370 --> 00:25:00.040
Next episode

00:24:56.370 --> 00:25:00.040
Battle of Gosroth

00:24:56.370 --> 00:25:00.040
Slachoth Gothlautr
